.TH LSCPU 1 "September 2026" "mitos-utils 0.1.0" "MITOS User Commands"
.SH NAME
lscpu \- print basic CPU information
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lscpu
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print CPU count, vendor ID, model name, clock speed, and cache size
from
.B /proc/cpuinfo
(Linux). A summary, not a full replica of the real
.BR lscpu (1)
-- cache topology, NUMA nodes, and CPU flags aren't covered.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Every mitos-utils command additionally accepts \fB\-\-help\fR and \fB\-\-version\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, non-zero if
.B /proc/cpuinfo
couldn't be read.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nproc (1),
.BR mitos\-box (1)
